    "evidence_text": "Peter DiFronzo\n\n and Joseph and John DiFronzo.\n\n He stands at 5'8 and weighs 185 pounds.\n\n Peter is also supposedly active in some of the Outfit's racketeering schemes.\n\nJoseph Andriacchi\n\nJoseph \"The Builder\" Andriacchi (born October 20, 1932) has been reported by Chicago newspapers to be a high-ranking member of the Chicago Outfit criminal organization.\n\nGenna crime family\n\nThe Genna crime family, was a Prohibition era crime family in Chicago.\n\n These brothers were Sicilians from the town of Marsala and operated from Chicago's Little Italy and maintained control over the Unione Siciliana.\n\n They were allies with fellow Italian gang the Chicago Outfit.\n\nJames LaPietra\n\n He was also the younger brother of mobster Angelo \"the Hook\" LaPietra.\n\nJames Marcello\n\n Marcello is the Cousin of Michael Hayes Marcello, and a cousin of Robert Urbinatti.\n\n He is also the father of Rocco Marcello.\n\nJoseph Lombardo\n\n He was alleged to be the Consigliere of the Outfit.\n\n He was considered \"Chicago's top labor racketeer\" in the 1950s.\n\n One high-ranking Chicago Teamsters leader noted in 1954, \"He is the mob.\n\n When he opens his mouth, it's the syndicate talking.\"\n\n A United States Senate committee once claimed that Glimco ran \"the nation's most corrupt union.\"\n\nAngelo J. LaPietra\n\n The victims most often died from suffocation.\n\nJohn DiFronzo\n\nChicago Outfit Roller Derby",
